{"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The shortest tour, by Held–Karp dynamic programming (Bellman, “Dynamic programming"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"treatment of the travelling salesman problem”, Journal of the ACM 9, 1962; Held and Karp,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"“A dynamic programming approach to sequencing problems”, Journal of SIAM 10, 1962): the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"least-weight Hamiltonian cycle of the simple graph, or nil when there is none; among the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"optimal ones, the lexicographically least by vertex number listed from the first vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(JGraphT "},{"code":"HeldKarpTSP","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s tour). The graph need not be complete: a missing pair is an absent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge. Tours read the simple graph, as "},{"code":"nearestNeighborTour(weight:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" documents; nil below"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"three vertices."}],"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Tours\/HeldKarp.swift#L186","fileName":"HeldKarp.swift"},"title":"shortestTour(weight:)","modules":[{"name":"Tours","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5ToursE12shortestTour6weight5Walks5CycleVy6VertexQz5Edges_5IndexQZGSgqd__ANXE_ts18AdditiveArithmeticRd__SLRd__lF","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"shortestTour"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A